# LockSmithPro — Lockpicking Service Manager

**Find customers, manage lockpicking requests, and keep track of your tips.**

LockSmithPro gives rogues a dashboard for running a lockpicking service. Monitor chat for requests, invite customers, manage your job board, and track earnings while you focus on opening boxes.

## What's New in 1.1.0

- **Phrase-triggered auto-invites:** Optionally invite players whose requests match your configured include keywords.
- **WoW Forever names:** Preserve both first names and surnames when inviting, whispering, and tracking customers. Characters with the same first name stay separate.
- **Memory improvements:** Reuse job cards and animations, limit the board to 100 customers, and clean up temporary tracking data.
- **Updated client APIs:** Add compatibility handling for current Retail, Classic Era, TBC Anniversary, MoP Classic, and WoW Forever clients.

The 1.1.0 build has passed automated simulations for these five client families. Live in-game validation is still pending.

## 🎯 Find and Manage Requests

- Monitor **Trade, General, LFG, Say, and Whisper**, with individual channel toggles.
- Set comma-separated **include and exclude keywords** to control which requests appear.
- Identify supported junkboxes and lockboxes from **item links**, independent of the item's displayed language. Keyword filters remain customizable for your language.
- See customer names, messages, and known box skill requirements on the job board.
- **Invite, Whisper, or Ignore** customers directly from their job cards.
- Keep the newest request per customer, up to **100 jobs**. Requests older than 30 minutes are removed when new ones arrive.

When the client exposes your lockpicking rank, LockSmithPro checks it against known box requirements. If no rank is available, it shows **Unknown** instead of incorrectly treating your skill as zero.

## 🤝 Optional Auto-Invites

Enable **Auto-invite matching requests** in the dashboard's Settings tab to invite customers when their messages match your include keywords. This feature is **off by default**.

Auto-invites respect enabled channels, exclusions, session ignores, recent trade partners, known skill requirements, group permissions, and cooldowns. Already-grouped players are skipped. Requests remain on the board if an invitation cannot be sent.

The separate **Auto-invite on Whisper** option can also invite non-matching whisper senders. Leave it disabled if you want invitations triggered only by matching phrases.

Invites have a **30-second cooldown per customer** and an additional limit across different customers. Automated communication depends on what the game client permits.

## 📊 Track Your Service

- Track **session and lifetime earnings**, job totals, and average tips.
- Keep **last-session and best-session earnings**.
- Count supported boxes received through trade and Pick Lock casts on the trade window's **“Will Not Be Traded” slot**.
- Record trade totals after the game confirms completion.
- Group repeat trades with the same customer within a **10-minute window** into one job.
- Keep full customer identities, including realms on realm-based clients and surnames in Forever.

## 📢 Advertise Your Service

Write your own advertisement and use `%SPELL_LINK%` to insert a Pick Lock spell link.

Choose **Trade, General, LFG, or Yell**, then click **Send Ad** or **Yell Ad**. The optional timer reminds you when an advertisement is ready; **it does not post automatically**. Advertisement channel lookup currently uses English channel names.

## 💬 Replies and Customer Tools

- Optional **low-skill replies** when an exposed skill rank is below a known box requirement.
- Customizable **thank-you whispers** after tipped trades, using `%TIP%` for the amount.
- Recent-trade tracking to reduce follow-up “thank you” requests on the board.
- Session ignores and group-member checks to avoid repeated requests.
- Optional **Star marker for yourself** and a preset sequence of raid markers for customers, subject to group permissions and client restrictions.
- Sound toggles, a draggable minimap button, and a resizable dashboard.

## Getting Started

1. Type **`/ls`** or left-click the minimap button to open the dashboard.
2. Open **Settings** and choose your channels, include keywords, and exclusions.
3. Click **Start** on the job board.
4. Review incoming requests and use **Invite**, **Whisper**, or **Ignore**.
5. Complete trades to update your statistics.
6. Optionally enable phrase-triggered invitations or set an advertisement reminder.

## Slash Commands

Use `/ls` or `/LockSmithPro` with these commands:

- `/ls` — Open the dashboard.
- `/ls start` — Start monitoring.
- `/ls stop` — Stop monitoring.
- `/ls toggle` — Toggle monitoring on or off.
- `/ls ad` — Submit your advertisement to enabled channels.
- `/ls skill` — Display your exposed lockpicking rank, or Unknown.
- `/ls stats` — Print earnings and job statistics.
- `/ls minimap` — Show or hide the minimap button.

To reset statistics, use **Reset Stats** in the dashboard's Statistics tab and confirm the prompt.

